{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-10-23T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Two grey wolves move through the sagebrush of Yellowstone National Park in Wyoming, home to some of North America's most closely watched wolf packs. Their thick coats help them withstand harsh winters, and their keen senses make them skilled hunters and communicators.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.YellowstoneWolves_EN-IN7964007510_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.YellowstoneWolves_EN-IN7964007510_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Partners in the wild","Title":"Two grey wolves, Yellowstone National Park, Wyoming, United States","Copyright":"© John Morrison/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Grey wolves can communicate through howls, body language, scent marking and a range of vocalisations, including barks, whines and growls.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261023_YellowstoneWolves\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Wolf+Awareness+Week&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261022_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261023_YellowstoneWolves"},"Ssd":"20261023","Name":"YellowstoneWolves","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7964007510","FullDateString":"23 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Few places in South Korea capture the magic of autumn quite like Naejangsan National Park, where mountainsides glow in brilliant shades of scarlet, orange, yellow and gold. Located in the country's southwest, the park is particularly famous for its vivid maple colours, making it one of Korea's premier destinations for autumn scenery. Its name, meaning 'many secrets in the mountains,' reflects the varied landscapes found throughout the region.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NaejangsanNP_EN-IN7823705566_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NaejangsanNP_EN-IN7823705566_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Still waters, vivid colours","Title":"Autumn in Naejangsan National Park, South Korea","Copyright":"© Twenty47studio/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/35.481191,126.889374/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=35.481191,126.889374;S9;Naejangsan National Park, South Korea&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261022_NaejangsanNP\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Naejangsan+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261021_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261022_NaejangsanNP"},"Ssd":"20261022","Name":"NaejangsanNP","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7823705566","FullDateString":"22 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Bridging the gap between old and new, Nguyen Hoang Bridge gives Hue's skyline a fresh connection. Spanning the Perfume River in Vietnam, the modern steel-arch landmark opened to traffic on 26 March 2025. Its design, called 'The Crane Facing Thien Mu,' draws inspiration from a local legend and nearby Thien Mu Pagoda.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VietnamBridge_EN-IN7535392593_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VietnamBridge_EN-IN7535392593_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Winging it over the river","Title":"Nguyen Hoang Bridge over the Perfume River, Hue, Vietnam","Copyright":"© VU PHAM VAN/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/16.455292,107.55998/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=16.455292,107.55998;S9;Nguyen Hoang Bridge, Hue, Vietnam&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261021_VietnamBridge\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Hue+Vietnam&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261020_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261021_VietnamBridge"},"Ssd":"20261021","Name":"VietnamBridge","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7535392593","FullDateString":"21 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Slow and steady wins the race—and the brown-throated sloth seems perfectly happy to skip the race altogether. On International Sloth Day, this three-toed mammal offers a different lesson in getting by: conserve energy, hang on and take your time.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BrownSloth_EN-IN7427775510_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BrownSloth_EN-IN7427775510_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Life in the slow lane","Title":"Brown-throated sloth, Puerto Viejo de Talamanca, Costa Rica","Copyright":"© Suzi Eszterhas/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/9.65531,-82.755699/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=9.65531,-82.755699;S9;Puerto Viejo de Talamanca, Limón, Costa Rica&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261020_BrownSloth\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=International+Sloth+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261019_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261020_BrownSloth"},"Ssd":"20261020","Name":"BrownSloth","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7427775510","FullDateString":"20 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Nine days of devotion, nine forms of Durga and one powerful finale—Maha Navami brings Navratri to its most intense stretch. Observed on the ninth day, it celebrates Goddess Durga's victory over the buffalo demon Mahishasura, earning her the name Mahishasuramardini, or slayer of Mahishasura. The day is also dedicated to Maa Siddhidatri, the ninth form of Navadurga, who is associated with spiritual powers and blessings.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MahaNavami2026_EN-IN6653933239_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MahaNavami2026_EN-IN6653933239_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"When Shakti rises","Title":"Goddess Durga idol in a pandal","Copyright":"© shouvik mondal/iStock/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"A 41.5-metre-tall Durga Puja pandal, modelled on Vrindavan's Chandrodaya Temple, earned a Guinness World Records title as the tallest pandal ever built.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261019_MahaNavami2026\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Maha+Navami&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261018_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261019_MahaNavami2026"},"Ssd":"20261019","Name":"MahaNavami2026","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"6653933239","FullDateString":"19 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"If parks could keep birthday diaries, Eryri National Park (Snowdonia) in Wales would have quite the story to tell. The park turns 75 today, marking the anniversary of its designation in 1951. Eryri stretches across more than 2,100 square kilometres, with nine mountain ranges, about 120 kilometres of coastline and habitats ranging from peatlands and native woodlands to upland landscapes. At more than 1,000 metres, Yr Wyddfa is Eryri's highest point. Nearby, the Carneddau and Glyderau add their own peaks, while Cadair Idris rises in the south. These protected landscapes provide habitats for wildlife and include 17 National Nature Reserves and 56 Sites of Special Scientific Interest.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DolbadarnWales_EN-IN6584156399_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DolbadarnWales_EN-IN6584156399_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"75 and thriving","Title":"Dolbadarn Castle, Llanberis, Eryri National Park (Snowdonia), Wales","Copyright":"© joe daniel price/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/52.927253,-4.077652/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=52.927253,-4.077652;S9;Eryri National Park, Wales&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261018_DolbadarnWales\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Eryri+National+Park+Wales&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261017_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261018_DolbadarnWales"},"Ssd":"20261018","Name":"DolbadarnWales","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"6584156399","FullDateString":"18 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some discoveries start with a shovel. Others start with a drawing on a cave wall. International Archaeology Day celebrates both the detective work and the evidence behind them. Organised by the Archaeological Institute of America, this annual event began in 2011 and became International Archaeology Day in 2013 as participation expanded worldwide. Today, it brings archaeology closer to the public through talks, museum programmes, site visits, simulated digs and hands-on activities.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ChauvetPaintingsFrance_EN-IN6496493041_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ChauvetPaintingsFrance_EN-IN6496493041_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":false},"Headline":"The past, unearthed","Title":"Life-size replica of Chauvet cave art in Vallon-Pont-d'Arc, France","Copyright":"© Audrey Poree/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"The Chauvet Cave preserves the footprints of a prehistoric adolescent who walked barefoot through its passages about 30,000 years ago.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261017_ChauvetPaintingsFrance\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=International+Archaeology+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261016_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261017_ChauvetPaintingsFrance"},"Ssd":"20261017","Name":"ChauvetPaintingsFrance","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"6496493041","FullDateString":"17 Oct, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Winter brings a familiar rhythm to Bosque del Apache National Wildlife Refuge in New Mexico. The cranes arrive, wetlands fill with birds, and this area becomes a hub for seasonal wildlife. Established in 1939, the 57,331-acre sanctuary was created to provide a protected stopover for migrating waterfowl. Its wetlands, fields and waterways now support wildlife throughout the year. Sandhill cranes, seen in today's image, are especially associated with the refuge during winter.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnCranes_EN-IN9113460841_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnCranes_EN-IN9113460841_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Time to fly high","Title":"Sandhill cranes, Bosque del Apache National Wildlife Refuge, New Mexico, USA","Copyright":"© Terry St.Louis/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/34.384147,-106.900263/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=34.384147,-106.900263;S9;Bosque del Apache National Wildlife Refuge, New Mexico&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261030_AutumnCranes\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sandhill+Cranes&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261029_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261030_AutumnCranes"},"Ssd":"20261030","Name":"AutumnCranes","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9113460841","FullDateString":"30 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As morning mist drifts among the standing stones of Avebury in Wiltshire, England, the scene feels almost timeless. These ancient megaliths form part of one of the world's most remarkable prehistoric landscapes, centred on a vast Neolithic monument built around 4,500 years ago. Avebury contains the world's largest prehistoric stone circle, as well as a massive henge and stone avenues extending into the surrounding countryside. Together with nearby monuments such as Silbury Hill and West Kennet Avenue, it forms part of an extensive Neolithic complex that has fascinated generations of visitors, researchers and archaeologists.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AveburyStones_EN-IN9660577333_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AveburyStones_EN-IN9660577333_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where mist meets millennia","Title":"Standing stones at Avebury in Wiltshire, England","Copyright":"© George W Johnson/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/51.42898,-1.854909/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=51.42898,-1.854909;S9;Avebury, Wiltshire, England&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261029_AveburyStones\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Avebury+henge+Wiltshire&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261028_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261029_AveburyStones"},"Ssd":"20261029","Name":"AveburyStones","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9660577333","FullDateString":"29 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What stories could these walls tell? Rising above eastern Bohemia in Czechia, Kunětická hora Castle has witnessed centuries of history. Dating to the late 14th century, the castle gradually evolved into an impressive fortress and noble residence. Its elevated position offered commanding views of the surrounding countryside and helped make it an important stronghold.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.KuneticeCastle_EN-IN9209042094_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.KuneticeCastle_EN-IN9209042094_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where history stands watch","Title":"Kunětická hora Castle, Bohemia, Czechia","Copyright":"© Marek Saroch/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/50.080287,15.811615/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=50.080287,15.811615;S9;Kunětická hora Castle, Czechia&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261028_KuneticeCastle\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Kuneticka+hora+Castle&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261027_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261028_KuneticeCastle"},"Ssd":"20261028","Name":"KuneticeCastle","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9209042094","FullDateString":"28 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Reflected in calm water and glowing in the light of the setting sun, this grove of pond cypress creates a striking display of colour and symmetry. Native to the southeastern United States, the species is associated with shallow ponds, depressions and wetland habitats. This image was captured in Georgia, where these trees can be found in places such as the Okefenokee Swamp and other low-lying wetlands.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PondCypress_EN-IN8944704657_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PondCypress_EN-IN8944704657_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Nature's golden mirror","Title":"A grove of pond cypress trees with autumn foliage, Georgia, United States","Copyright":"© Chris Moore/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Pond cypress can develop knobby root structures known as 'knees' that rise above the water or soil around the tree.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261027_PondCypress\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Pond+cypress&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261026_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261027_PondCypress"},"Ssd":"20261027","Name":"PondCypress","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8944704657","FullDateString":"27 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Bulgaria's Western Rhodope Mountains, autumn leaves gather beside the rushing waters of Sitovo Waterfall. Near the village of Sitovo, southwest of Plovdiv, the falls tumble beneath an old stone bridge whose arch frames the cascades like a storybook scene. Moss-covered stones and pine trees add shades of green to the autumn landscape, while fallen leaves gather along the water's edge or drift through its pools. The falls become especially lively after rain and during spring snowmelt, when the surrounding woodland echoes with the sound of rushing water.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SitovoWaterfall_EN-IN8441319721_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SitovoWaterfall_EN-IN8441319721_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Nature's autumn soundtrack","Title":"Autumn waterfalls near Sitovo, Plovdiv Province, Bulgaria","Copyright":"© Nadya85/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/41.926863,24.615841/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=41.926863,24.615841;S9;Sitovo, Plovdiv Province, Bulgaria&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261026_SitovoWaterfall\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sitovo+Plovdiv+Bulgaria&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261025_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261026_SitovoWaterfall"},"Ssd":"20261026","Name":"SitovoWaterfall","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8441319721","FullDateString":"26 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What if a city's busiest street had no road? In Venice, Italy, traffic flows along the Grand Canal, a 3.9-kilometre waterway that winds through the city in a giant reverse S-shape. Known to locals as the Canalazzo, it is Venice's main water-traffic corridor, carrying vaporetti, water taxis, gondolas, police boats and other vessels. The canal follows the course of an ancient river that once flowed into the Venetian Lagoon.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VeniceSunrise_EN-IN8305689376_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VeniceSunrise_EN-IN8305689376_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The road that runs on water","Title":"Grand Canal in Venice, Italy","Copyright":"© Juan Romero/Cavan Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/45.435337,12.32783/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=45.435337,12.32783;S9;Grand Canal, Venice, Italy&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261025_VeniceSunrise\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Grand+Canal+Venice&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261024_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261025_VeniceSunrise"},"Ssd":"20261025","Name":"VeniceSunrise","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8305689376","FullDateString":"25 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today we're inside the Royal Portuguese Cabinet of Reading in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, where the humble act of opening a book took on grand architectural ambitions. Founded in 1837 by 43 Portuguese immigrants, just 15 years after Brazil's independence, the institution eventually moved into the building seen here, completed half a century later in a lavish Neo-Manueline style. Shelves soar over 20 metres around a vast reading room, crowned by a monumental stained-glass skylight that makes daylight part of the design.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PortugueseLibrary_EN-IN8235557432_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PortugueseLibrary_EN-IN8235557432_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":false},"Headline":"Bookishly extravagant","Title":"Royal Portuguese Cabinet of Reading, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil","Copyright":"© Antonio Salaverry/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-22.905431,-43.182116/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-